 ## Background
-The technique was introduced to overcome the impracticality of collecting paired clinical data (2D X-ray and 3D CT) in medical settings [S2]. It leverages the TIGRE tomography toolbox for accurate projection geometry [S2] and SimpleITK for robust medical image I/O [S1, unofficial]. The method is commonly used in research involving Neural Radiance Fields (NeRF) and other deep learning models for medical image reconstruction [S1, unofficial][S2].
+The technique was introduced to overcome the impracticality of collecting paired clinical data (2D X-ray and 3D CT) in medical settings [S2]. It leverages the TIGRE tomography toolbox for generating X-ray images [S2] and SimpleITK for loading medical image volumes [S1, unofficial]. The method is commonly used in research involving Neural Radiance Fields (NeRF) and other deep learning models for medical image reconstruction [S1, unofficial][S2].
 
